+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` looks at trades within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), starting from the most recently closed trade and walking backwards in time. It counts how many of those trades lost money **in a row** - the count stops as soon as a trade that wasn't a loss is found. Unlike `StoplossGuard` or `LowProfitPairs`, this is not about how many losses happened within the window overall, but specifically about an unbroken losing streak.
+
+If `trade_limit` or more losses happened consecutively, trading will stop for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+This applies across all pairs (pausing new entries bot-wide) as well as per pair, unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, which will then only lock the specific pair that had the losing streak, leaving other pairs free to trade.
+
+For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side, allowing for example shorts to continue after a series of losing longs.
+
+`required_profit` determines the relative profit (or loss) below which a trade counts as a "loss" for the streak. This should normally not be set and defaults to 0.0 - meaning any non-profitable close breaks even and counts towards the streak.
+
+The below example stops trading (both for the affected pair, and bot-wide) for 4 candles after 3 losing trades happened back-to-back within the last 24 candles.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 4,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+            "only_per_side": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
+!!! Note
+    Set `only_per_pair: true` if you only want the affected pair locked, without pausing entries bot-wide.
+    `trade_limit` and `lookback_period` will need to be tuned for your strategy.
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
